summary='''# Parallel Peg physics and paired skill-value learning — 2026-11-03

**Independent RL method gain: UNVERIFIED.** Start commit 0a93740, clean workspace, remote fetched and already current. ARES-R read-only, network-isolated simulation, GPU0 only, no sealed tests or site data.

## What changed scientifically

This round implemented and trained one explicit mechanism, then tested its competing explanations and connected it to native tasks. It did not rename a controller fix as RL. Ordinary SAC, matched-value differences, generic absolute supervision and shuffled pairs share observations, legal actions and training data. The candidate is preserved as negative evidence.

PegInsertionSide-v1 retains the official 100-step horizon and native success: peg-head x >= -15 mm and y/z within the native hole radius. Geometry, task initialization and success thresholds are unchanged. The pinned official helper obtains a CPU world OBB; under this GPU setup that pose is stale (example grasp target z=100 mm versus actual peg center z=16 mm). The literal official GPU invocation and all failed compatibility attempts are retained. An adapter uses the same local collision OBB with the actual GPU actor pose, without setting physical states. This is a shared compatibility correction, not learning.

With the corrected geometry, original official timing scores 1/6. A separately labeled shared retiming (planner velocity/acceleration multipliers 2.0 instead of .75) scores 3/6. It preserves all official screw planning and three refinement passes; no skipped path samples. It is a native-task controller variant, not an unchanged official-solver score or real-robot dynamics certification. Preliminary retiming and direct-insert attempts before correcting geometry are invalid as learning-opportunity evidence and retained as diagnostics.

Freeze this shared controller before the parameter experiments. Two decisions are real: choose a longitudinal grasp offset {-10,0,+10} mm before physical pick/align, then choose original or actual-attachment terminal target from the measured handoff before INSERT. The first option includes grasp, transport and alignment; the second is insertion. Native geometry varies naturally by scene. Ten design scenes / 60 complete trials produce best fixed 6/10 and observed parameter union 8/10. The union is an oracle, not a deployable result. Exact-prefix checks demonstrate both rescues and regressions. On 750103, the same -10mm grasp has an identical 75-step prefix; attachment refresh changes final head x from -111.6 mm to +34.1 mm and native failure to success. On a new scene, the previously best configuration regresses. Thus parameter consequences are real and conditional, but not an algorithm gain.

## Algorithm implementation and three actual research loops

1. Scene-group cross-validation on the existing 190 Tool episodes (23 scenes, 38 grasp contexts; 26 reach the postcontact decision). Ordinary two-stage Fitted Q, matched-pair consistency, shuffled/unpaired control, direct supervised outcome, mean-suffix-value analogue and discrete STAP-style Q-product/dynamics were trained, 600 updates, three training seeds and three scene folds. Terminal critic inputs are identical across baselines; FQI/supervised/foresight differ in predecessor targets, not six independent successor models. Paired consistency improves ranking only 162/180 to 163/180 repeated discordant comparisons, with unchanged selected success. No gain.
2. Competitive explanation: equal-outcome pairs dilute the learning signal. Training only discordant differences makes joint selection worse (34/69 versus ordinary 36/69); equally weighted absolute mixed-label training reaches 36/69. This excludes that sampling change as an improvement on this dataset.
3. Integrate the SAME contrast loss into inherited masked LN-SAC critic gradients, without adding a head. Actor/critic update counts and capacity are matched; all-data auxiliary backprop has extra computation, disclosed in TRAINING.json. At 200 updates, logged closed-candidate whole-chain selection is ordinary32/69, paired40/69, absolute38/69, shuffled39/69. At1200: ordinary44/69, paired43/69, absolute44/69, shuffled42/69. These are 23 scene groups repeated across three train seeds, not69 independent scenes. Same data and closed candidate projections apply to all; this is not fresh physics or proof of sample efficiency. The shuffled RNG caveat is in PRIOR_ART_COMPARISON.md.

The prototype was then reused on the actual Peg two-option data. Scene-group FQI: ordinary18/30 versus paired16/30 joint selections (10 scenes ×3 train seeds). This also does not support independent gain. Both stages have one effective scalar action. Peg SAC explicitly masks the unused second coordinate in BOTH critic and entropy, rather than transferring the Tool two-dimensional successor entropy. Runtime projects grasp to the same three legal offsets and insertion to the same two target choices for every learned method. Full-data Peg SAC has118 real option transitions from60 physical episodes; this is a working bounded baseline, not sufficient convergence evidence.

## Fresh physical evaluation (new development, not sealed)

| Native task | Ordinary SAC200 /1200 | Paired SAC200 /1200 | Absolute auxiliary | Strong fixed |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Tool100, six scenes748200–205 |3/6 /3/6|3/6 /3/6|3/6 (200)|3/6|
| Peg100, four scenes750140–143 |2/4 /2/4|2/4 /2/4|2/4 (1200)|2/4 (both fixed choices)|

Tool additionally evaluates shuffled200, also3/6. Full-data training seed31201; no claim of multi-seed physical superiority. New controller, new task distribution and auxiliary objective are individually identified. Learning uses only train trajectories, never future labels during execution. All positive and negative checkpoints remain.

Peg failures 750140 and750143 both acquired a grasp. One ends without reaching insertion depth; the other exhausts its native budget. Reconstructing the target using the actual attachment gives approximately +50mm goal-axis displacement in both failed and successful cases (TARGET_SEMANTICS.json), ruling out a reversed commanded frame in those examples. Actual motion can still stall in contact. Contact-force cause is not established: this Peg logger records poses, joint velocities, grasp and native outcomes but not force histories. Do not label this proven wedging or train on an invented force signal.

## Costs, provenance and reproducibility

ANALYSIS.json independently SHA-checks all160 complete episodes /16000 control steps, including6 instrumentation-error episodes (600 terminal-hold steps), which are excluded from valid controller conclusions. One startup assignment error occurred before environment construction (zero physics). Value optimizers:75600 joint update iterations. SAC:51600 actor and51600 critic updates across all folds, seeds, ablations and full-data runs; do not sum overlapping checkpoint counters. No online training interaction is hidden: training here reuses recorded physics, with fresh complete physical evaluation separately reported. Training.json files retain wall times, counts and checkpoints200/600/1200 (FQI200/400/600). Peg motion-call timings combine planning and execution; isolated planning CPU latency and Peg policy latency were not measured. Tool policy query timings are saved. This prevents falsely precise cost comparisons.

All43 SAC buffers were independently reconstructed from actual source physics with observation/action/reward/done error below1e-6 (BUFFER_AUDIT.json). All public trajectories, source snapshots, buffers, weights, negative runs and SHA are in RAW_MANIFEST.json archives. Prior-art restricted source is not republished; only pin/hash facts and analysis are included. Original official solver snapshots carry the ManiSkill Apache license. Restore using the existing restore_post_contact_evidence.py --package THIS_DIRECTORY --out NEW_DIRECTORY --portable; then run analyze_peg_value_loop.py --root NEW_DIRECTORY. Portable JSON relocation preserves original metadata and never rewrites physical gzip files or model weights.

Important executable sources: program_peg_native.py; program_paired_skill_value.py; program_skill_value_sac_control.py; evaluate_paired_sac_physics.py; analyze_peg_value_loop.py; render_peg_skill_pair.py. Each run stores its execution snapshot. Training changed in later loops; replay the snapshot corresponding to a historical model, not an arbitrary latest version.

Video: full101 frames (initial plus100 steps),20fps, measured-state replay, no new physics. RAW means unannotated measured-pose rendering, not a camera recording. The English axial version and clickable synchronous curves use identical records. Static frames and encoding were inspected; browser playback interaction is not claimed automatically verified. Original lateral-only rendering is retained as a visualization revision, not another experiment.

## Research decision

RETAINED: GPU OBB adaptation, strong common Peg executor, actual two-option SkillResult interface, exact-prefix comparisons, ordinary masked SAC and the minimal critic-contrast implementation with controls. LOCAL_NEGATIVE: matched return differences, focusing discordant pairs, and their SAC auxiliary do not yield independent task gains. OPEN_MECHANISM: naturally varying Peg conditions produce different useful grasp/handoff choices, while the remaining failure includes contact tracking and finite budget despite correct target semantics. Ordinary RL is operational but not declared sufficiently converged from118 Peg transitions.

Next experiment should distinguish an executable contact correction from a purely predicted successor advantage on the common Peg controller: measure actual contact/axial progress and remaining budget, then compare a bounded reapproach/hold primitive against a strong shared geometry/feedback baseline. Keep the same critic prototype for a controlled continuation if new paired data genuinely change decision value; do not restart a collection of renamed auxiliary heads or treat the old closed-set early advantage as novelty. The primary paper question remains task-conditioned multi-stage executable skill RL. EXP-003 shared-baseline and EXP-004 method work continue together. No independent contribution is established yet.
'''
